---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PhotoSlot from '../components/PhotoSlot.astro';
import { digestParagraphs, lastUpdatedHuman } from '../data/now';

const title = 'Adrian Watkins. Operator. Builder. Governor.';
const description = 'Adrian Watkins. Senior commercial and governance operator across Asia-Pacific and Europe. 25 years. Creator of the EDGE Framework for Applied Intelligence. SVP Commercial Operations and Governance, SQREEM Technologies.';

// Person + WebSite JSON-LD is emitted globally via BaseLayout
// (src/data/person.ts). No need to duplicate here.
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} current="home">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-text">
          <div class="eyebrow">Singapore. 25 years across Asia and Europe.</div>
          <h1>Operator. Builder.<br /><em>Governor.</em></h1>
          <p class="lede">Senior commercial and governance leadership for organisations adopting AI seriously. Creator of the EDGE Framework for Applied Intelligence.</p>

          <div class="manifesto prose">
            <p>I have spent 25 years building and governing commercial businesses across Asia-Pacific and Europe. The last five have been about one question. Why do most organisations adopt AI like they are buying stationery, then act surprised when nothing compounds?</p>

            <p>I built EDGE to answer that question for the teams I work with, and to give boards a working language for AI capability that does not collapse the first time someone asks "but what did it actually do?".</p>

            <p>I am SVP of Commercial Operations and Governance at SQREEM Technologies. I sourced and led the integration of the TotallyAwesome acquisition in 2024. I also publish <a href="https://aiinasia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AIinASIA.com</a>, which reaches around 10,000 readers a month without paid distribution, and I built <a href="https://promptandgo.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PromptAndGo.ai</a> because Asia deserves AI prompts that respect the register, the market, and the language.</p>

            <p>If you are a CEO, a board chair, or a sponsor and you need someone who can carry the commercial number and the governance memo in the same week, I take on a small number of advisory, fractional, and non-executive engagements a year. The rest of this site explains how.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="ctarow">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Book a 30-minute call</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/edge">Read the EDGE framework</a>
          </div>

          <div class="meta-line">
            <span>SVP, <a href="https://sqreem.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SQREEM Technologies</a></span>
            <span>Advisor, <a href="https://blackstormco.asia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BlackStorm Group</a></span>
            <span>Coach, <a href="https://beyond4.tech/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Beyond4Tech</a></span>
            <span>Publisher, <a href="https://aiinasia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AIinASIA.com</a></span>
            <span>Moderator, <a href="https://ortusclub.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ortus Club</a></span>
            <span>Builder, <a href="https://promptandgo.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PromptAndGo.ai</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="hero-photo">
          <img src="/images/hero-portrait.jpg" alt="Adrian Watkins. Black-and-white editorial portrait. Singapore." />
          <figcaption>Singapore, 2025.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Selected work.</h2>
        <p class="aside">Three named engagements where the public record speaks for itself. The longer list, with anonymised cases, sits on the work page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cases">

        <article class="case">
          <div class="tag">M&amp;A integration, 2024</div>
          <h3>SQREEM acquires TotallyAwesome.</h3>
          <p>I sourced the target, helped broker the deal, and led the go-to-market and operational integration. Two commercial stacks became one, with governance controls in place from day one. The internal lessons sit in the EDGE Govern pillar.</p>
          <div class="meta">Public commentary on the acquisition is on record.</div>
        </article>

        <article class="case">
          <div class="tag">Owned media, since 2020</div>
          <h3><a href="https://aiinasia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AIinASIA.com</a>.</h3>
          <p>I founded and publish <a href="https://aiinasia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AIinASIA</a>, an editorial brief on how artificial intelligence is actually being adopted across Asia-Pacific. Around 10,000 readers a month, zero paid distribution, written for operators rather than tourists.</p>
          <div class="meta"><a class="meta-link" href="https://aiinasia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aiinasia.com</a></div>
        </article>

        <article class="case">
          <div class="tag">Advisory, since 2020</div>
          <h3>BlackStorm Group.</h3>
          <p>Advisor on growth, transformation, and AI adoption for BlackStorm's Asia-Pacific portfolio of founders and scale-ups. Workshops, board prep, and the harder conversations about which AI initiatives to stop.</p>
          <div class="meta"><a class="meta-link" href="https://blackstormco.asia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">blackstormco.asia</a></div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>How I work.</h2>
        <p class="aside">Four engagement shapes. I take on a small number of each per year. Selection happens both ways.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="help">
        <div class="help-card">
          <h4>One</h4>
          <h3>EDGE Diagnostic.</h3>
          <p>A 25-minute structured conversation that produces a board-ready snapshot of where your AI adoption actually is. The output is a single-page memo, not a slide deck.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="help-card">
          <h4>Two</h4>
          <h3>Fractional leadership.</h3>
          <p>Embedded commercial and governance leadership on a defined cadence. For founders and operators who need a senior peer, not a consultant.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="help-card">
          <h4>Three</h4>
          <h3>Advisory and board.</h3>
          <p>Non-executive, advisory board, or specific board-committee work. AI governance, commercial readiness, and the hard parts of Asia-Pacific go-to-market.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="help-card">
          <h4>Four</h4>
          <h3>Capability workshops.</h3>
          <p>One-day and multi-day executive workshops built on the EDGE pillars. Outputs are working artefacts your team uses on the Monday after.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="edge" class="dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 style="color:#F4ECD8">The EDGE Framework.</h2>
        <p class="aside" style="color:#B7A98E">A practical structure for applied intelligence. Four pillars. Used by founders, operators, and boards.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="edge-quote">Artificial intelligence is widely accessible.<br /><em>Structured capability is not.</em></p>

      <div class="pillars">
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="num">01</div>
          <h3>Evaluate.</h3>
          <p>Where you actually are. Capability, exposure, and the gap between what your AI tools do and what your teams say they do.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="num">02</div>
          <h3>Define.</h3>
          <p>What "good" looks like for your organisation. The specific outcomes AI is allowed to chase, and the ones it is not.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="num">03</div>
          <h3>Govern.</h3>
          <p>The decisions, controls, and review cadence that turn AI activity into AI capability. Board-legible. Not theatre.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <div class="num">04</div>
          <h3>Elevate.</h3>
          <p>What changes about your people, your operating model, and your competitive position when the first three are in place.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ctarow" style="margin-top:48px">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/documents/EDGE-Framework-Whitepaper.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="background:#D89A55;color:#1A1714">Download the EDGE white paper</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/edge" style="border-color:#E9E2D2;color:#E9E2D2">Try the EDGE Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:#F4ECD8;opacity:0.92;margin-top:18px;max-width:none">Tools and diagnostic live on <a href="https://democratising.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">democratising.ai</a>. Built on the EDGE Framework.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="now-grid">
        <div class="label">
          <h2><a href="/now" class="now-heading-link">/now.</a></h2>
          <p>What I am working on this quarter. Updated monthly. Borrowed from Derek Sivers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="body">
          {digestParagraphs.map((p) => (<p>{p}</p>))}
          <p class="now-cta"><a href="/now" class="now-cta-link">Read the full /now log →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="writing" class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>More of me.</h2>
        <p class="aside">Five places to go deeper.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="slots">

        <article class="slot">
          <div class="kicker">Weekly</div>
          <h3>Friday Frame.</h3>
          <p>A 200-word frame on what I noticed this week. Operators, governance, Asia-Pacific. Cross-posted to LinkedIn, archived here.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/writing/friday-frame">Read the archive</a>
        </article>

        <article class="slot">
          <div class="kicker">Quarterly</div>
          <h3>Reading list.</h3>
          <p>Five books a quarter, one line each, with the date I picked them up. The Patrick Collison move. Current: Heffernan, Levinson, Slouka, Tett, McGilchrist.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/now#reading">Read the list</a>
        </article>

        <article class="slot">
          <div class="kicker">Long-form</div>
          <h3>Essays and cross-posts.</h3>
          <p>The canonical executive writing. LinkedIn Pulse essays archived here, plus <a href="https://aiinasia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AIinASIA</a> cross-posts that earn a longer read.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/writing">Read the essays</a>
        </article>

        <article class="slot">
          <div class="kicker">This quarter</div>
          <h3>/now.</h3>
          <p>What I am working on this quarter. Updated monthly. Borrowed from Derek Sivers and the nownownow.com convention.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/now">See what is current</a>
        </article>

        <article class="slot">
          <div class="kicker">Stage and panel</div>
          <h3>/speaking.</h3>
          <p>Recent and upcoming keynotes, panels, and moderation. Selected engagements across Asia-Pacific and beyond.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/speaking">See the calendar</a>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="speaking">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Recent and upcoming.</h2>
        <p class="aside">Selected engagements. Full calendar on the speaking page.</p>
      </div>

      <PhotoSlot
        src="speaking-government.jpg"
        alt="Adrian Watkins on stage opening the Taipei City Government Smart Living, Sustainable Future 2025 event."
        description="Adrian opening the Taipei City Government keynote at Smart Living, Sustainable Future 2025."
        aspectRatio="16 / 9"
        caption="Opening keynote, Smart Living, Sustainable Future 2025. Taipei City Government, November 2025."
      />

      <div class="speak">
        <div class="speak-card">
          <div class="when">November 2025</div>
          <h3>Smart Living, Sustainable Future 2025.</h3>
          <p>Guest of Taipei City Government. Opened the event with "Democratising Intelligence for a Sustainable Future" and moderated the startup panel. <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/your-ai-earning-its-energy-taiwan-has-left-me-adrian-watkins-uzvgc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Post-event reflection on LinkedIn Pulse.</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="speak-card">
          <div class="when">From May 2026</div>
          <h3>SDG Open Hack 2026, NP Edition.</h3>
          <p>Mentor on the Ngee Ann Polytechnic edition of SDG Open Hack 2026. Running across the hack window and beyond.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta alt" id="contact">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Ready for a real conversation about AI?</h2>
      <p class="lede">I am selective about what I take on. A 30-minute call is the right place to start, even if we conclude we are not a fit.</p>
      <div class="ctarow">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Book a 30-minute call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/documents/AdrianWatkins_Executive-CV.pdf?v=12" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Download my executive CV</a>
      </div>
      <p class="quiet" style="margin-top:24px;font-size:13px">I typically respond within two business days. Singapore-based, available across Asia-Pacific time zones.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
